                "senderName": "NWS State College PA",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued September 4 at 12:05PM EDT until September 5 at 8:00AM EDT by NWS State College PA",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of central Pennsylvania, including the following\ncounties, Bedford, Blair, Cambria and Somerset.\n\n* WHEN...Through 8 AM Saturday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of creeks,\nstreams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations. Creeks and\nstreams may rise out of their banks. River flooding is also\npossible.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Training heavy showers and embedded thunderstorms will track\nsoutheast across the region this afternoon into tonight. Rainfall\nrates of 1 to 2 inches per hour will be possible. Heavy rain\nfalling at this rate will lead to rapid runoff and flash\nflooding, as rainfall rates required to result in flash flooding\nare only 0.75 to 1.25 inches over a one hour period across the\nwatch area. Localized storm total rainfall this afternoon through\ntonight could reach 3 inches in some locations, mainly to the\nsouth of Interstate 76.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "Please monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action should\nFlash Flood Warnings be issued.",
                "response": "Prepare",
                "note": null,
